eported applied, without deriving safety from proposal-admission asymmetry alone.',map_path='core-map-v2-refined.json',map_changes=changes,sources=newsrc,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['19745caf3e0c46ad96c930eb5730f723','0f9e8d1e51f64b34a017f21c8f359d94','conf-proposal-contract','leader-admit','mode-contract','membership-doc'],answered='The local read-release result is retained separately in its reviewed check. New source observation: stepLeader considers a configuration pending iff pendingConfIndex exceeds reported raftLog.applied, whereas joint-state checks and commit quorums use installed trk.Config. Node.ProposeConfChange documents dropping changes unless no prior unapplied change exists; Config documentation also warns these checks have false positives and false negatives and are best-effort. confchange.Simple validates each applied change against installed configuration and restricts voter symmetric difference to one. These statements are preserved together: an admitted second change alone would not prove agreement failure or violation of an unconditional validation promise.',remaining=['Construct a legal synchronous Node history with delayed leader application, successive simple removals, and later partitioned proposals/elections; observe actual committed entries rather than infer safety from differing configurations.','Determine whether per-entry application, vote freshness, Step membership filters or current-term commitment prevent the proposed divergence.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The highest-value next discriminator is committed-prefix agreement across the stale-configuration leader and the newly configured participant. Actual producer histories and public Node calls can test alternate protections; source comments about best-effort admission are not enough to establish or dismiss that safety relation.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.ins